    "text": {
     "en": "(additional, not in the textbook) Seeds must spread away from the mother plant to find space to grow.\nSome seeds, like dandelion, fly with the wind. Coconuts float on water. Some seeds stick to animals' fur, and birds eat fruits and drop the seeds.\nA seed grows into a new plant when it gets water, air and warmth.\nPlant a seed and watch it grow."
